Your 7-Day Dubai Trip Itinerary

Day 1: Arrival and Exploring Downtown Dubai

* Morning: Arrive at Dubai International Airport and take a taxi or metro to your hotel
* Afternoon: Visit the Burj Khalifa observation deck ( tickets start from AED 125 per person) for breathtaking views of the city
* Evening: Explore the Dubai Mall, one of the largest shopping malls in the world, featuring over 1,200 stores, ice skating rinks, and a variety of dining options

Day 2: Desert Safari and Traditional Emirati Cuisine

* Morning: Take a desert safari tour (starting from AED 150 per person) that includes dune bashing, camel riding, and a relaxing campsite experience under the stars
* Evening: Enjoy traditional Emirati cuisine at Al Mallah restaurant (machboos, luqaimat, etc.) and explore the Souk al Bab marketplace

Day 3: Palm Jumeirah and Luxury Shopping

* Morning: Visit the Palm Jumeirah island, home to several luxury hotels, beaches, and attractions like the Dubai Fountain Show
* Afternoon: Shop at the Atlantis, The Palm (starting from AED 100 per person) or other luxury shopping malls on the island
* Evening: Enjoy a beachside dinner at the Jumeirah Beach Restaurant

Day 4: Cultural Experiences and Water Activities

* Morning: Visit the Sheikh Zayed Mosque (tickets start from AED 25 per person), offering guided tours for non-Muslims
* Afternoon: Take an Abra ride (starting from AED 1.5 per person) across the Dubai Creek, exploring the city's rich history and culture
* Evening: Relax on Kite Beach or try water sports like kayaking or paddleboarding

Day 5: Museum of the Future and Traditional Turkish Cuisine

* Morning: Visit the Museum of the Future (tickets start from AED 30 per person), showcasing cutting-edge technology and architecture, featuring interactive exhibits and a stunning dome-shaped design
* Afternoon: Enjoy traditional Turkish cuisine at At.mosp restaurant (menemen, lahmacun, etc.) or explore other dining options in the area

Day 6: Global Village and Relaxation

* Morning: Visit the Global Village (tickets start from AED 30 per person), featuring pavilions from over 90 countries, offering a glimpse into international traditions and cuisines
* Afternoon: Relax at your hotel or explore nearby attractions like Jumeirah Lakes Towers
* Evening: Enjoy a British-inspired dinner at Dukes Tavern

Day 7: Departure

* Morning: Spend some time shopping for last-minute souvenirs or exploring any remaining attractions
* Afternoon: Depart for the airport and fly back home

Practical Travel Tips:

* Best time to visit: November to March for mild weather and fewer tourists
* Currency: UAE Dirham (AED)
* Language: Arabic, but English is widely spoken
* Safety: Be mindful of traffic rules, as driving in Dubai can be challenging
* Tipping culture: Optional, but rounding up bills or leaving 10% is considered polite

Remember to check the current entry requirements, visa regulations, and any COVID-19 measures before your trip. Enjoy your time in Dubai!


